stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Capture
    Capture --> CaptureRejected: Invalid address including length limits, source, time, or inactive party
    Capture --> ContactUnconfirmed: Valid address is absent from complete stored tokens
    Capture --> ContactExact: Valid address equals a complete normalized stored token
    Capture --> CaptureFailed: Database or envelope fails
    CaptureFailed --> [*]: Caller receives failure
    CaptureRejected --> [*]: No activity is written
    ContactUnconfirmed --> StageProposed: Eligible factual contact needs confirmation
    ContactExact --> StageProposed: Other strong evidence is missing
    ContactExact --> StageAppliedWithExistingStrongEvidence: Existing stage policy accepts all evidence
    ContactExact --> NoStageChange: Automated, delayed future, unrelated, or stale evidence
    ContactUnconfirmed --> NoStageChange: Evidence is ineligible
    StageProposed --> [*]: Human approval remains required
    StageAppliedWithExistingStrongEvidence --> [*]: Existing job records provenance and sends nothing
    NoStageChange --> [*]
    %% never exact-match a substring, shared domain, display name, or malformed token
    %% never qualify from an exact contact alone without existing strong evidence
    %% capture is synchronous; it introduces no background work or teardown
    %% address limits are 254 ASCII octets total, 64 local-part octets, and 63 octets per domain label
